Here's the TUnit lifecycle at each scope:

---

### 1. Before/after every test in a class

```csharp
public class OrderTests
{
    [Before(Test)]
    public async Task ResetDatabase(TestContext context)
    {
        await InMemoryDb.ResetAsync();
    }

    [After(Test)]
    public async Task Cleanup(TestContext context)
    {
        // optional per-test teardown
    }

    [Test]
    public async Task Order_WithNoItems_Throws() { /* ... */ }
}
```

---

### 2. Once before/after all tests in a class (class-scoped fixture)

```csharp
public class PaymentGatewayTests
{
    [Before(Class)]
    public static async Task OpenFixture(ClassHookContext context)
    {
        // runs once before the first test in this class
        await SharedFixture.InitAsync();
    }

    [After(Class)]
    public static async Task DisposeFixture(ClassHookContext context)
    {
        // runs once after the last test in this class
        await SharedFixture.DisposeAsync();
    }

    [Test]
    public async Task Charge_Succeeds() { /* ... */ }
}
```

> Methods must be `static` for class/assembly/session hooks.

---

### 3. Once before/after all tests in the assembly

```csharp
public static class WireMockSetup
{
    [Before(Assembly)]
    public static async Task StartServer(AssemblyHookContext context)
    {
        await WireMockServer.StartAsync();
    }

    [After(Assembly)]
    public static async Task StopServer(AssemblyHookContext context)
    {
        await WireMockServer.StopAsync();
    }
}
```

---

### 4. Once at the very start/end of the entire test session

```csharp
public static class GlobalDatabaseMigration
{
    [Before(TestSession)]
    public static async Task ApplyMigrations(TestSessionContext context)
    {
        await Database.MigrateAsync();
    }

    [After(TestSession)]
    public static async Task TearDown(TestSessionContext context)
    {
        await Database.DropAsync();
    }
}
```

---

### Quick reference

| Scope | Before | After | Method must be |
|-------|--------|-------|----------------|
| Each test | `[Before(Test)]` | `[After(Test)]` | Instance |
| Class | `[Before(Class)]` | `[After(Class)]` | `static` |
| Assembly | `[Before(Assembly)]` | `[After(Assembly)]` | `static` |
| Session | `[Before(TestSession)]` | `[After(TestSession)]` | `static` |

**Bonus — global cross-cutting hooks** (run for *every* test/class across the entire run, not just one class):

```csharp
[BeforeEvery(Test)]
public static async Task LogStart(TestContext ctx) { /* ... */ }

[AfterEvery(Test)]
public static async Task LogEnd(TestContext ctx) { /* ... */ }
```

All hooks optionally accept the matching context object and/or a `CancellationToken`.
